ses offered in Academic Programs 2022-2023a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2021-2022a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2020-2021a.y. Close Career Services Section Menu Overview Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Overview Career Guidance Approaching the Job Market Meet with employers Overview Bespoke events Career fairs JobGate: applying online Your internship: from start to recognition Overview Guide to curricular internships Guide to extracurricular internships Close Breadcrumb Home For Current Students Career Services Contacts Career Services Open share Close Share Facebook X Email WhatsApp LinkedIn Close Bocconi Career Services support students and graduates as they enter the job market , providing tools and advice to help them reach their professional goals. Close ties with the business community and organizations have enabled successful partnerships with employers , allowing the recruitment of qualified talents . With the goal of fostering contacts between students and employers worldwide, Bocconi Career Services organize a portfolio of activities related to recruiting, networking and career counseling , available throughout the academic year. Available Career Services Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Tools and initiatives to support your first approach to the job market Meet with employers Meet with single employers on bespoke events, or engage with a range of employers during career fairs JobGate: applying online Bocconi’s online portal to find an internship or a job Your internship: from start to credit recognition Activate and manage your internship with the support of Bocconi's Internship Office Placement of Bocconi Graduates 94.7% MSc graduates employed 1 year after graduation 36% employed abroad Bocconi and Employers in 2025 16 career fairs in Italy and abroad, with 700+ participating employers 740+ employers involved in meetings with students and graduates 9,300+ internship and job opportunities posted online Associ