    "https://www.unibocconi.it/en/employers-and-partners/jobgate-internship-and-job-posting": {
      "title": "JobGate: internship and job posting",
      "description": "JobGate: internship and job posting | Bocconi University Skip to main content What are you looking for? Languages EN IT Menu Close Apply Discover Programs Browse News and Events Giving to Bocconi About Us Overview Organization Quality Assurance Third Mission Ranking International Networks Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Sustainability Community Programs Overview Bachelor of Science Master of Science Law Specialized Masters Programs PhD Summer School SDA Bocconi School of Management Faculty and Research Faculty Departments Research Campus Overview Campus VR Virtual Tour Buildings and Classrooms On-Campus Safety and Security Information Security Library & Archives Bocconi Sport Gallery Applying to Bocconi Overview Bachelor and Law Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Specialized Master Programs PhD Programs Summer School Post-Experience Education News and Events Hub Overview Events ViaSarfatti25 - Our Magazine Research Dissemination For Current Students Overview Welcome Days Bachelor Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Application and Admissions Campus Life Career Services Fees Funding Guidance for MSc Programs Guide to the University Housing Inclusion, Disabilities and Learning Disorders International Mobility IT Education Center Language Center Library & Archives Student Administration Technology and Information Services Timetables, Calendars and Rooms Courses offered in Academic Programs 2026-2027 a.y. For International Students Overview Prospective students - Before your admission Freshly enrolled students - Before you arrive Freshly enrolled students - When you arrive Current students Incoming Exchange Students For Employers and Partners Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Career fairs Bespoke events For Alumni Contact us Login Languages EN IT Close menu For Employers and Partners Section Menu Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Overview Focus on Curricular vs Extracurricular Internships How to start an internship Career fairs Bespoke events Close JobGate: internship and job posting Section Menu Overview Close Breadcrumb Home For Employers and Partners JobGate: internship and job posting Contacts JobGate: internship and job posting Open share Close Share Facebook X Email WhatsApp LinkedIn Close JobGate is Bocconi University's job portal available to employers for posting internship and job offers , managing applications , and accessing the University's graduate database (CVBook). JobGate is also the tool to start internship agreements with selected students and graduates: for info related to this topic, please check the web pages dedicated to internship documents . 2025 wrapped 3,900+ Active companies in JobGate posting offers or hosting internships 9,300+ Internship and job opportunities in Italy or abroad, posted on JobGate Discover more How to register To access JobGate, recruiters need to register at: employers.unibocconi.it During registration, employers need to upload in the system standard information (company name, website, registered and operative office, company contact), as well as a company presentation and a certificate of incorporation (if available). At the end of registration, the recruiter will receive the credentials via email: a contact, either by phone or email, from a Bocconi Account - Employer Relationship Manager, is required to unblock the password and is aimed at sharing the general understanding of the system's functioning, the advertisement publication methods, and the company's recruitment needs. To use this service, the employer must accept the General Conditions that regulate the portal. How to access To access JobGate, recruiters must enter their credentials at: employers.unibocconi.it Passwords are strictly personal and cannot be transferred to third parties. All company contacts needing access to the portal can register by clicking on \"Registration of a new contact\" to obtain their credentials. Posting offers Employers can publish both internship and placement offers. Internship announcements can be dedicated to: Current students (curricular internships) Graduates up to 12 months after graduation (extracurricular internships). For more information on the employer's role and responsibilities in the internship relationship (tutor, internship modality, educational project, etc.), you can visit the pages dedicated to activating and managing internships . Job announcements can be dedicated to: Junior profiles (positions requiring up to 3 years of experience) Senior profiles (positions requiring more than 3 years of experience). The use of JobGate is free, and companies can post as much offers as they wish. The only exception is for Head Hunting Agencies, which can publish job offers for themselves and for client companies only, and internship offers for themselves only: in both cases, the limit is 12 offers per year (maximum of 2 offers simultaneously). CVBook The CVBook Directory is the online database of CVs of Bocconi University graduates . The access is from the JobGate portal, and employers can use filters to sort results according to objective criterias. DAL Project - Disabilities and Work The DAL Service- Disabilities and Work supports companies in identifying and hiring Bocconi students and graduates belonging to Protected Categories. In particular, the service offers the possibility of posting dedicated internship and job offers on JobGate and notifies candidates with the specific requirements . Additionally, Bocconi University has joined C.A.L.D. (Coordinamento Atenei Lombardi per la Disabilità) with the aim of undertaking joint initiatives with Lombard universities to sustain the employment of students and graduates with disabilities. Contacts Please check the General Conditions regulating the access and use of the system, as well as the FAQ for a better user experience. For general info: employer.relations@unibocconi.it For tech support: help.jobgate@unibocconi.it Scroll to top Stay in touch Contacts Stay in touch Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Tiktok Weechat Xiaohongshu/RED Listen to our podcast Spotify Spreaker Apple podcast Bocconi Spheres SDA Bocconi School of Management Egea Alumni B4i - Bocconi for innovation yoU@B Agenda Work at Bocconi Media center BTV TL ON Mobile app yoU@B Campus VR Mobile app yoU@B Bocconi shop © Università Bocconi - Via Sarfatti, 25 Milano - PI 03628350153 Footer Privacy Digital accessibility Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More… × Notice We   and selected third parties   collect personal information as specified in the privacy policy and use cookies or similar technologies  for technical purposes and, with your consent, for functionality, experience, measurement and “marketing (personalized ads)” as specified in the cookie policy . You can freely give, deny, or withdraw your consent at any time by accessing the preferences panel.  Denying consent may make related features unavailable. Use the “Accept” button to consent. Use the “Reject” button or close this notice to continue without accepting. Press again to continue 0/1 Learn more and customize Reject Accept"
    },
    "https://www.unibocconi.it/en/employers-and-partners/career-fairs": {
      "title": "Career fairs",
      "description": "Career fairs | Bocconi University Skip to main content What are you looking for? Languages EN IT Menu Close Apply Discover Programs Browse News and Events Giving to Bocconi About Us Overview Organization Quality Assurance Third Mission Ranking International Networks Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Sustainability Community Programs Overview Bachelor of Science Master of Science Law Specialized Masters Programs PhD Summer School SDA Bocconi School of Management Faculty and Research Faculty Departments Research Campus Overview Campus VR Virtual Tour Buildings and Classrooms On-Campus Safety and Security Information Security Library & Archives Bocconi Sport Gallery Applying to Bocconi Overview Bachelor and Law Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Specialized Master Programs PhD Programs Summer School Post-Experience Education News and Events Hub Overview Events ViaSarfatti25 - Our Magazine Research Dissemination For Current Students Overview Welcome Days Bachelor Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Application and Admissions Campus Life Career Services Fees Funding Guidance for MSc Programs Guide to the University Housing Inclusion, Disabilities and Learning Disorders International Mobility IT Education Center Language Center Library & Archives Student Administration Technology and Information Services Timetables, Calendars and Rooms Courses offered in Academic Programs 2026-2027 a.y. For International Students Overview Prospective students - Before your admission Freshly enrolled students - Before you arrive Freshly enrolled students - When you arrive Current students Incoming Exchange Students For Employers and Partners Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Career fairs Bespoke events For Alumni Contact us Login Languages EN IT Close menu For Employers and Partners Section Menu Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Overview Focus on Curricular vs Extracurricular Internships How to start an internship Career fairs Bespoke events Close Career fairs Section Menu Overview Close Breadcrumb Home For Employers and Partners Career fairs Contacts Career fairs Open share Close Share Facebook X Email WhatsApp LinkedIn Close Bocconi's career fairs are one of the main channels through which companies can connect with students and graduates and gain great visibility on campus . Different formats are available, depending on the focus of the events: there are career fairs dedicated to specific sectors or open employers from all fields, or dedicated to particular Countries. In all cases, employers are welcome to showcase their internship and job offers , interact with participants online or in presence, and collect applications . 2025 wrapped 2 editions of Bocconi&Jobs 285 participating employers, 6,200+ participating students and graduates 7 career fairs dedicated to specific business fields 300 participating employers, 4,200+ participating students and graduates 7 editions of Bocconi&Jobs abroad 160+ participating employers, 1300+ participating students and graduates Discover more Bocconi&Jobs: the main career fair With two editions each year, in Spring and Fall, it is the main career fair of the University, open to employers from all business fields and Countries. During the event, companies, organizations, and law firms are welcome to meet students and graduates to promote internship and job opportunities, identify and select ideal profiles, and boost their employer brand. Participation in the event is subject to a fee. For further info: bocconi.jobs@unibocconi.it Bocconi&Jobs abroad: the career fairs dedicated to specific countries Eight editions per year dedicated to speci fic geographical areas: Benelux, DACH, France, Luxembourg, Middle East, Spain and Portugal, UK and Ireland (two editions per year). Th ese career fair s are dedicated to companies offering internship and job opportunities in specific countries. The aim is to facilitate contacts between the local branches of companies and those students interested in internship or job opportunities in some of the main international markets, towards which candidates have a strong motivation. For further info: bocconiandjobsabroad@unibocconi.it Investment Banking Days: the career fair dedicated to Investment Banking Orientation and recruiting event dedicated to the world of Investment Banking, traditionally held at the beginning of the fall semester. The initiative allows companies to join a series of professional guidance activities (career workshops and round tables) to help students better understand the field and prepare for submitting applications. It is also possible to interact with students and graduates and showcase recruiting programs and available opportunities. Participation is reserved for Corporate Associates . For further info: ibw@unibocconi.it Recruiting Dates: the career fairs dedicated to specific business fields Recruiting events dedicated to employers from specific business fields, with the aim to meet students and graduates for networking and promoting available internship and job opportunities. The Recruiting Dates are organized for the following sectors: Arts, Sport & Entertainment; Banking, Financial Services & Fintech; Fashion, Luxury & Beauty; Government, Public Services & International Organizations; Web & IT Companies. For further info: recruiting.date@unibocconi.it Tax&Legal Networking Event: the career fair dedicated to Law & Tax Firms On campus networking and recruiting event, exclusively dedicated to Law Firm Associates . For further info: employer.relations@unibocconi.it Scroll to top Stay in touch Contacts Stay in touch Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Tiktok Weechat Xiaohongshu/RED Listen to our podcast Spotify Spreaker Apple podcast Bocconi Spheres SDA Bocconi School of Management Egea Alumni B4i - Bocconi for innovation yoU@B Agenda Work at Bocconi Media center BTV TL ON Mobile app yoU@B Campus VR Mobile app yoU@B Bocconi shop © Università Bocconi - Via Sarfatti, 25 Milano - PI 03628350153 Footer Privacy Digital accessibility Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More… × Notice We   and selected third parties   collect personal information as specified in the privacy policy and use cookies or similar technologies  for technical purposes and, with your consent, for functionality, experience, measurement and “marketing (personalized ads)” as specified in the cookie policy . You can freely give, deny, or withdraw your consent at any time by accessing the preferences panel.  Denying consent may make related features unavailable. Use the “Accept” button to consent. Use the “Reject” button or close this notice to continue without accepting. Press again to continue 0/1 Learn more and customize Reject Accept"
    },
